WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:04.310
Everything in the Marvel Cinematic Universe
has slowly been building up to the arrival

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.700
of Thanos, and after years of waiting, Avengers:
Infinity War is finally here.

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.740
Which raises just one big question for superhero
fans: now what?

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:17.020
Of course, Marvel has already allegedly created
a meticulous master plan that runs through

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.140
the year 2028.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:21.500
But since they aren't telling anyone what
they have in mind, we'll just have to look

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:25.720
at the clues to figure out just how Infinity
War will change the MCU forever.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.840
Expect departures

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:32.740
The contractual obligations for many of the
stars of the MCU end with Avengers: Infinity

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:33.240
War.

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:37.080
Rumors and reports have circulated for years
that some of the MCU's biggest stars would

00:00:37.090 --> 00:00:41.159
be unwilling to renew, with Robert Downey,
Jr., Chris Evans, and Chris Hemsworth all

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:45.440
stating at various times that they were planning
to leave the MCU at the end of their contracts.

00:00:45.530 --> 00:00:48.760
Of course, people can change their minds,
and being offered hundreds of millions of

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:50.000
dollars often helps.

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.549
But considering pretty much every Marvel superhero
was killed in the Infinity Gauntlet comic

00:00:54.549 --> 00:00:58.299
book series that Infinity War is based on,
it would seem like Marvel has been planning

00:00:58.299 --> 00:01:02.179
the perfect sendoff for the current version
of the MCU - and the current lineup of stars

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:02.940
- for years.

00:01:03.220 --> 00:01:07.860
While most are signed through the Infinity
War follow-up in 2019's Avengers 4, chances

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:12.020
are pretty good that Infinity War is at least
the beginning of the end for everything you've

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.560
known and loved about the MCU for the past
decade.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:17.100
Expect new arrivals

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.800
If the thought of losing your favorite superheros
is a big ol' bummer, don't worry, because

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:24.890
Marvel has plenty of other characters waiting
in the wings for their closeup.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:28.840
Sure, some of the characters left in their
stable may not be as famous as their current

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:32.250
line-up, but be honest: had you ever heard
of the Guardians of the Galaxy before they

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.360
became the coolest thing in any universe?

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.800
What about Doctor Strange, or Ant-Man, or
even Iron Man?

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:42.670
Yes, hard as it may be to remember now, but
Iron Man was once considered a second string

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:47.210
hero, and featuring him in his own solo film
was regarded as a massive risk when the first

00:01:47.210 --> 00:01:48.940
Iron Man film came out a decade ago.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:53.520
So don't worry if you've never heard of Moon
Knight, Brother Voodoo, or Shang-Chi, Master

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.320
of Kung-Fu.

00:01:54.520 --> 00:01:58.240
Because given Marvel's track record, chances
are they'll be your new favorite character

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.120
before the final credits finish rolling.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.240
Expect more diversity

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:06.909
The undeniable critical and commercial success
of Black Panther should be enough to convince

00:02:06.909 --> 00:02:11.250
even the most doubtful cynic that after Infinity
War, we should expect to see Marvel Studios

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.980
doubling and tripling down on its commitment
to diversity.

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:18.220
Starring mostly actors of color, written and
directed by people of color, Black Panther

00:02:18.230 --> 00:02:22.440
proved — if nothing else — there's no
good reason to shy away from Marvel's collection

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:23.700
of more diverse heroes.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:27.940
With the success of Black Panther, the highly
anticipated Captain Marvel waiting in the

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.620
wings, Avengers: Infinity War's ensemble cast
featuring numerous people of color and women,

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:37.280
the persistent whispers of a solo Black Widow
movie, and a still largely untapped reserve

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.220
of Marvel comics characters waiting for their
names to be called, Marvel movie fans should

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.700
expect to not only see more women heroes and
heroes of color, but their real-life counterparts

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.540
writing and directing.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:48.980
Expect more laughs

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:52.020
Marvel movies are funny, and they'll continue
to be funny.

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:56.040
Though the Avengers franchise, which sits
at the heart of the MCU, has been a deadly

00:02:56.050 --> 00:03:00.400
serious affair with deep real-world themes
and moral debates, it's also been laced with

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.300
all sorts of funny gags and light asides.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.600
[Sound of a body being repeatedly slammed
into the ground]

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.500
"Puny god."

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.700
Unlike the DC Extended Universe, films in
the MCU are actually fun to watch, and as

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:21.790
films like Guardians of the Galaxy and Thor:
Ragnarok have proven, the more audiences laugh,

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:24.100
the more money they're likely to spend seeing
it again.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.950
Thor: Ragnarok was even so fun that star Chris
Hemsworth reportedly has been reconsidering

00:03:28.950 --> 00:03:30.720
his decision to leave the MCU.

00:03:30.820 --> 00:03:35.320
And all that added humor helped Thor: Ragnarok
earn not just the most money of the three

00:03:35.320 --> 00:03:38.280
Thor films, but also the best reviews.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.520
In fact, one of the few criticisms of the
movie was that it might have been too funny!

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:47.200
Given the success of Ragnarok in revitalizing
one of Marvel's key franchises, though, don't

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:51.960
expect the laughs to stop any time soon, especially
with Ant-Man and the Wasp and Guardians of

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:54.320
the Galaxy vol. 3 already in the pipeline.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:59.000
The events of Infinity War may be sad, but
chances are, Marvel has a plan to turn that

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.320
frown upside down sooner rather than later.

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.580
Expect more variety

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.610
Maybe the biggest secret to Marvel's success
is the fact that while they seem to be making

00:04:07.610 --> 00:04:11.670
superhero movies, they're actually making
movies from all sorts of different genres

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.320
that just happen to feature superheroes as
the main characters.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.260
Think about it.

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.360
Captain America: Winter Soldier was a classic,
70's style espionage movie.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:24.210
Guardians of the Galaxy was a space opera,
while Doctor Strange and Thor: The Dark World

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:25.240
were fantasy films.

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:29.960
Ant-Man was a heist flick, while Ant-Man and
the Wasp has been described as a romcom, and

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:33.560
Spider-man: Homecoming was their take on the
classic John Hughes high school dramedy.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:38.120
It's that non-formula formula that has worked
so well for Marvel up until this point, so

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:42.220
fans should expect to see more of the same
- by expecting less of the same when it comes

00:04:42.220 --> 00:04:43.160
to Infinity War.

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.740
Marvel isn't going to follow up their big
smash em up epic action crossover with more

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:48.240
of those.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:52.680
Instead, they're likely to branch out even
further, picking characters that work well

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:53.900
in different types of films.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:55.700
Want to see a Marvel western?

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:57.620
They've got the Two-Gun Kid for that.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:58.990
A Marvel horror movie?

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.680
How about Simon Garth, the Zombie?

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.000
A Marvel war movie?

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:03.380
Hello, John Kowalski!

00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.620
It sounds weird, but Marvel plays it safe
by not playing it safe, so going forward,

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:10.840
expect even more variety than we've gotten
so far.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:13.060
Expect more space

00:05:13.460 --> 00:05:17.020
One of the corners of the Marvel Universe
that has found nothing but success is the

00:05:17.020 --> 00:05:17.520
cosmos.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:20.080
Both Guardians of the Galaxy films were hits.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:24.530
And, like humor, the cosmic element added
to Thor: Ragnarok was a key ingredient to

00:05:24.530 --> 00:05:25.820
turning around the franchise.

00:05:25.980 --> 00:05:30.680
While the first Avengers brought us an alien
invasion, Avengers: Infinity War promises

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:34.260
an even stronger attachment to Marvel's cosmic
mythology than ever.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.740
With Quasar, Nova, Adam Warlock, Moondragon,
and more, there are almost as many heroes

00:05:39.740 --> 00:05:42.560
among the stars as there are on Marvel's Earth.

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:46.080
And the possible acquisition of Fox's properties
opens even more doors.

00:05:46.260 --> 00:05:51.360
The Fantastic Four are cosmic explorers, and
the Silver Surfer is the ultimate cosmic hero.

00:05:51.480 --> 00:05:55.480
Considering all the success Marvel has had
in space, and the fact that its audience is

00:05:55.490 --> 00:06:00.040
now familiar enough with its cosmic mythology
to not burden future films with extraneous

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:05.420
explanations, there is no reason to think
Marvel won't explore other far out franchises.

00:06:05.860 --> 00:06:08.000
Expect complete Annihilation

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:14.150
So what will Marvel's next giant film crossover
event be once Infinity War and Avengers 4

00:06:14.150 --> 00:06:14.900
have come and gone?

00:06:15.150 --> 00:06:19.680
Well, if Marvel does use Infinity War and
the acquisition of the Fantastic Four and

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:24.810
the Silver Surfer as an excuse to launch even
more cool outer space movies, the next logical

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:26.820
step is complete Annihilation.

00:06:27.140 --> 00:06:30.980
That's because in the comics, while the Earth-bound
heroes were all busy fighting each other with

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:35.770
their Civil War thing, Marvel's space heroes
were engaged in a galaxy-spanning Armageddon

00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:39.560
called Annihilation, with the Guardians of
the Galaxy leading the way.

00:06:39.980 --> 00:06:44.880
With Infinity War bringing the alien menace
to Earth, the next logical step for our heroes

00:06:44.880 --> 00:06:46.980
is to take that fight back into space.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:51.580
Of course, Marvel has plenty of other massive
crossover storylines they could do instead,

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:56.979
but given the popularity of their sci-fi franchises
- and the space connections evident in 2019's

00:06:56.980 --> 00:07:01.400
Captain Marvel, which seems set to include
the space war between the Kree and the Skrull

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:03.900
- Annihilation seems like the safest bet.

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:05.800
Expect the X-Men

00:07:06.500 --> 00:07:11.520
Finally, the acquisition of Fox would provide
the MCU with the most obvious new direction.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:15.540
Now that the threat from without has been
taken care of, what about the threat from

00:07:15.540 --> 00:07:19.400
within posed by the emergence of a mutant
population hiding among us?

00:07:19.540 --> 00:07:24.280
With the Avengers potentially gone, who could
possibly stand up to the danger of…

00:07:24.280 --> 00:07:25.360
The X-Men?!

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:30.360
It's inevitable that the X-Men will play a
major role in the MCU once Disney has rights

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:32.920
to the characters, we just don't know yet
how it will play out.

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:38.720
Will Thanos use the reality-warping Infinity
Gauntlet to somehow merge the MCU with Fox's

00:07:38.720 --> 00:07:39.720
X-Men universe?

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:44.000
Or will the characters develop organically,
with the X-Men franchise getting rebooted

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:48.510
completely - like Spider-man was - so that
the emergence of the mutant menace becomes

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:51.460
the cornerstone of Marvel's next Phase, and
beyond?

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:56.250
However Marvel ends up bringing the X-Men
into the MCU, once they are there, there's

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.260
no question that they're going to be at the
center of everything that follows - and not

00:08:00.260 --> 00:08:01.620
necessarily as heroes.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:06.760
Could the MCU follow the comics by having
Cyclops become the big bad guy in a race war

00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.120
between humans and mutants?

00:08:08.360 --> 00:08:11.500
In a world without the Avengers as we know
them, anything is possible.

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:13.300
Thanks for watching!

00:08:13.480 --> 00:08:15.820
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:18.020
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

